// Retail 0x0049D660, 787 B. This reconstruction is now 787/787 B with 147
// non-relocation byte differences, and every one of them is the POSITION of
// two constant materialisations inside one straight-line region:
//
//   +0x3d  retail: mov dword ptr [esi + 0x28], ebx   ours: xor eax, eax
//   +0x9a  retail: xor eax, eax                     ours: (end of ebx chain)
//   +0x114 retail: mov dword ptr [esi + 0x60], ebx   ours: mov eax, 0x64000000
//   +0x132 retail: mov eax, 0x64000000               ours: (inside the ebx group)
//
// The two 20- and 12-entry zeroing runs are MSVC 7.1 if-converted loops; the
// constant their stores share is emitted at the TOP of the basic block that
// contains the run. Retail has a basic-block boundary at +0x9a (after the
// 17-store 0x28..0x268 chain) and another at +0x132 (after the seven-store
// 0x60/0x1c/0x18/0x2c8/0x29c/0x298/0x24 group), so both constants sit at the
// top of a smaller block. Ours has one block from +0x3d, so both constants
// sink to +0x3d and +0x114.
//
// Measured and ruled out as a way to open those two blocks (all keep 787 B and
// both constants hoisted, or shrink the body): the mem-initializer list (MSVC
// 7.1 emits it BEFORE the class-type member subobject constructors, so the
// chain cannot move there and still follow the +0x2d/+0x37 member stores);
// nested braces; forward goto to an adjacent label; dead `for`/`while(0)`/
// `do{}while(0)`/`if(0)`/`switch(0)`; `__asm{}` (empty is deleted, and
// `__asm{mov eax,eax}` costs 2 B and drags the EH state store to +0x3d);
// volatile members (destroys the if-conversion: 601 B real loop); inline free
// and member helpers, `__forceinline`, a local temporary with a constructor;
// `volatile`-qualified loop and colour members; a dedicated/unsigned/dedecrement
// induction variable, `i += 1`, `i != 20`, pointer-walk and `while` forms, and
// spelled zero values (`i - i`, `i & 0`, `(i, 0)`, `-0`, `(int)0`,
// `GameMakeColor(0,0,0,0)`). A two-distinct-store loop (10 x 2 entries) DOES
// move the first divergence to +0x9a, but then MSVC reuses ebx and emits no
// `xor` at all, so it cannot be the retail shape either.
//
// A positive lever found this session (kept below): the tail
// `f2f0 = new Gen_004B1670; f2f0->init();` must go through a local pointer.
// Reloading the member (`f2f0->init()`, or a local that is then re-read through
// `f2f0`) emits `mov ecx,eax` / `mov [esi+0x2f0],eax` / `mov edx,[ecx]`; with
// `Gen_004B1670 *p = new Gen_004B1670; f2f0 = p; p->init();` MSVC orders the
// member store first and then builds the dispatch receiver, giving retail's
// `mov [esi+0x2f0],eax` / `mov edx,[eax]` / `mov ecx,eax` / `call [edx+4]`.
// That removed 9 further differences (156 -> 147).
//
// Next lever to try: find the source construct that splits the body block
// after the 0x268 store and after the 0x24 store. blocker=codegen-order
// t=70min model=opencode/space-bunny-free

